# Deliberate bugs, one at a time: each (name, file, old text, new text) must make the suite fail.
# Run from apps/web:  python3 test/mutation/mutate.py test/mutation/mutants.py -- npx vitest run --bail 1
# (the driver checks the suite is green first; do not edit the tree while it runs; each pattern must occur exactly once)
#
# Not listed, because they cannot change behaviour:
#  - paths.isProxyablePath: the `segments.length === 0` guard (an empty path joins to "", which no allowed pattern matches; the guard states the intent);
#  - sse.applyStreamLine: `.slice(6)` -> `.slice(5)` (the payload is trimmed after), and dropping `parsed &&` (JSON "null" then fails on the
#    destructuring, and the surrounding catch returns the same skip);
#  - auth/refresh.refreshTokens: dropping `!response.ok` (an error body is not a token pair either, so the result is the same null);
#  - bff route: `request.method === "HEAD"` (no HEAD handler is exported);
#  - paths.safeNext: three checks that overlap on purpose, each of which makes another redundant for the same inputs, so dropping any one alone changes nothing:
#    the leading `//` test (the origin comparison refuses it too), the origin comparison (once control characters, backslashes and a leading `//` are refused, a
#    value starting with one `/` can only resolve to this site), and a backslash by itself (the parser reads "/\\evil.test" as "//evil.test", which the origin
#    comparison refuses). They are independent layers on the one check that stops an open redirect, so all three stay;
#  - tokens.isTokenPair, sse.applyStreamLine: the `typeof ... === "object"` that follows a truthiness check (reading a property of a number or a string gives
#    undefined, so the result is the same; the check says what the code means);
#  - config.apiBase: the localhost fallback (tests always set API_INTERNAL_URL for the code under test; the fallback is for local development).

